# University BE Backend Conventions

## Multi-tenancy (strict)

- Use **only** `scoped(model).findAll|findOne|findByPk|findAndCountAll|count|create|bulkCreate|update|destroy`.
- Never call model methods directly; never use `applyMultiTenancy()` or monkey-patch models.
- Tenant WHERE merge order — **scope must win**:


where: { ...options.where, ...baseWhere }  // baseWhere from buildScope last


- On `create` / `bulkCreate`, inject tenant fields from `buildScope()` filtered by `model.rawAttributes` only.
- Academic year / institute / university come from `buildScope(model)` + auth `requestContext` — not manual `requestContext.getStore()` defaults in function params.

## Keep code minimal

- Prefer **direct query keys** (`employeeId`, `sessionId`, `page`, `limit`) — avoid extra resolve/format helper layers.
- Do **not** split into many intermediate constants (`subjectWhere`, `mappingWhere`, `queryOptions`, `include`).
- Inline `where` / `include` inside `scoped(...).findAll` or `findAndCountAll`.
- Service layer: thin — pass `req.query` / `req.body` to repository; re-export repo reads when needed; no pass-through wrappers.
- Controller → service/repo only; business queries live in **repository**.

## Repository query pattern

// ✅ GOOD — scoped, buildScope on includes, inline query, paginated
const { rows: result, count: totalCount } = await scoped(model.teacherSubjectMappingModel).findAndCountAll({
  where: { ...(employeeId && { employeeId }) },
  include: [{
    model: model.subjectModel,
    as: 'employeeSubject',
    where: { ...(subjectId && { subjectId }), ...buildScope(model.subjectModel) },
    required: true,
  }],
  offset: (page - 1) * limit,
  limit,
  distinct: true,
  col: 'teacher_subject_mapping_id',
});

return { result, totalCount, page, limit, totalPages: Math.ceil(totalCount / limit) };

// ❌ BAD — manual year default, named query constants, double findAll+count
acedmicYearId = requestContext.getStore()?.academicYearId
const subjectWhere = { ...(acedmicYearId && { acedmicYearId }), ...buildScope(...) };


- Filter by academic year via `buildScope(model.subjectModel)` / `buildScope(model.classSectionModel)` on related includes.
- Use `X-Academic-Year-Id` header / token default (auth middleware) — do not duplicate year from query unless explicitly required.
- List endpoints return `{ result, totalCount, page, limit, totalPages }`.

## Routes

- Validate with Zod `validate({ body|query|params })` on write routes and list filters.
- Use distinct REST paths per resource (e.g. `DELETE /teacher/teacherSubject/:id`, not shared `/:id`).
- Keep Postman `docs/postman/univ-v2.postman_collection.json` in sync when routes or response shapes change.
